# No line-end conversion anywhere (Git for Windows converts to CR LF by default): the tools hash their own files and the profiles' tables byte for byte (the rewrite key,
# DMSH_CHAIN, DMSH_VK_CHAIN, the profile inputs digest), so a checkout on Windows must hold the Mac's bytes, or its packs and shader libraries are of another version
* -text
# The games gallery's table (dm/tools/docs_gallery.py writes docs/nxnative.md's gallery from it): a new game is a row at its end. docs/nxnative.md itself is not merged this way; after a
# conflict in its gallery, run docs_gallery.py. test_docs fails on a game in the table twice
docs/images/gallery.tsv merge=union
# Windows scripts keep CRLF line ends (cmd.exe misreads some LF-only batch files)
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
